<title>LATVIA: LATVIA-NOON RADIO HEADLINES-AUGUST 6.</title>
<headline>LATVIA-NOON RADIO HEADLINES-AUGUST 6.</headline>
<dateline>RIGA 1997-08-06</dateline>
<text>
<p>These are the main headlines on Latvian state radio at noon. Reuters has not verified these reports and does not vouch for their accuracy:</p>
<p>- The heads of leading political parties signed the new government's declaration, aiming at speeding reforms and entering the European Union.</p>
<p>- Central bank head Einar Repshe said the main achievement of outgoing prime minister, Andris Shkele, was to pass a balanced budget through parliament.</p>
<p>- A joint Latvian-Russian committee is meeting to discuss border questions.</p>
<p>-- Riga newsroom, +371 721 5240</p>
</text>
